stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Symptom
  Symptom: What you are seeing. States are named by SYMPTOM because that is the text the router matches against your prompt

  Symptom --> NixInvisibleFile: setup.sh or nix flake check fails right after adding or renaming a file
  NixInvisibleFile --> [*]: ROOT CAUSE nix flakes only see git-tracked files, so an untracked file does not exist inside the sandboxed build. FIX run git status --short and git add it, staging is enough. Do NOT reach for nix log, rebuild or keep-failed until this is ruled out

  Symptom --> BashBlocked: Blocked, that binary is not on the Bash allowlist
  BashBlocked --> [*]: ROOT CAUSE bash-allowlist-guard.sh is allowlist-only and inspects every command position, so shell keywords like for and while are refused too. FIX use the Read, Edit, Write and search tools, or add the binary to ~/.claude/bash-allowlist or .claude/bash-allowlist

  Symptom --> EditBlocked: PreToolUse refused an Edit or Write
  EditBlocked --> [*]: ROOT CAUSE boilerplate-guard.sh matched a boilerplate content signature and renaming the file does not exempt it, or pre-tool-use-edit-guard.sh saw an edit that changes nothing. FIX generate the file with scaffold_* then fill logic above the scaffold:inject marker

  Symptom --> ConfigReverted: an edit under $HOME vanished or came back as NAME.hm-backup
  ConfigReverted --> [*]: ROOT CAUSE managed files are read-only nix store symlinks and every apply forcibly re-links them. FIX make the change in this repo and run ./setup.sh, use ./setup.sh doctor to confirm no drift remains

  Symptom --> WslGarbage: escape sequence garbage in the terminal under WSL
  WslGarbage --> [*]: ROOT CAUSE extended-keys mode corrupts output on WSL, fixed in commit fe6ae64. FIX detect WSL and skip extended-keys rather than changing the terminal

  Symptom --> IconOffCenter: nerd font icon renders off-center or overlapping in Alacritty or VTE
  IconOffCenter --> [*]: ROOT CAUSE PUA glyphs carry Unicode Ambiguous width so the cell advance is wrong. FIX A/B test the same slot with a plain ASCII character to confirm it is width and not the font, then adjust the width setting

  Symptom --> WrongDiagram: the injected system map is wrong, stale or missing for a prompt
  WrongDiagram --> [*]: ROOT CAUSE routing is a case-insensitive substring match where the highest priority wins and exactly ONE file is injected, so a broad high-priority keyword can starve a specific route. FIX add the phrase you actually typed to that route in .ai-memory/manifest.json and check no higher-priority route already swallows it

